      "intro": "A Power Functions receiver channel is shared by its red and blue outputs. Two receivers using the same channel/output address hear the same command; decide whether that sharing is intentional.",
      "notes": [
        {
          "heading": "Eight command addresses, not eight guaranteed working motors",
          "text": "Official LEGO guidance describes four selectable channels and two output controls per channel. The planner maps channel × red/blue only. It does not validate power, receiver load, motor count, battery condition, infrared reach or simultaneous handset operation."
        },
        {
          "heading": "A collision is about independent intent",
          "text": "By default Receiver 1 and Receiver 2 both put different train groups on channel 1 red, so the plan conflicts. Move the second group to channel 1 blue to declare two separate addresses. Give both red outputs the same group name only when you intentionally want the same commands broadcast to them."
        },
        {
          "heading": "One receiver has one channel setting",
          "text": "Both output colors on one receiver use that receiver’s channel; they cannot each select a different channel. A handset selects one channel at a time. Several remotes on different channels can supply controls simultaneously, but this worksheet does not model operator actions or timing."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Sharing an address is not mechanically synchronized motion",
          "text": "Matching group labels on the same address mean deliberate command sharing. They do not establish equal motor speed, direction, torque or safe coupled movement. A group appearing on different addresses still needs separate commands; repeating its name does not electrically or wirelessly link those addresses."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Keep the declared area complete",
          "text": "The worksheet accepts up to six receivers in one shared IR-control area. More than four receivers can intentionally share addresses; four channels is not a four-receiver limit. If your area has more than six receivers, this finite worksheet cannot rule out omitted collisions. Group names ignore case and surrounding spaces; blank outputs are unused. This PF map is not Powered Up BLE pairing, older train IR, or a third-party RF addressing map."
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "LEGO — Running trains at the same time",
          "url": "https://www.lego.com/en-gb/service/help-topics/article/running-trains-at-the-same-time"
        },
        {
          "title": "LEGO Power Functions IR Remote Control 8885",
          "url": "https://www.lego.com/en-us/product/lego-power-functions-ir-remote-control-8885"
        }
      ]
